brief:
Implement §3.1, §3.4 and §4 of DESIGN-stellar-contracts-v2.revised.md.
- Add 11 workspace members: the 10 v2 contract crates (launchpad-v2, launch-token-v2, exec-soroswap, exec-aquarius, qa-exec-fail, lp-locker, moments-v2, moment-nft, moment-coin, moments-graduator) and a test-only integration-tests crate. Leave the v1 crates launchpad, launch-token and moments byte-for-byte untouched.
- dyor-common (§4):
  - types: VenueKind (Soroswap, Aquarius, HoldOnly, QaFail), VenueParams, GraduateArgs, GraduateResult, Payee, HarvestPayees {quote: Vec<Payee>, base: Vec<Payee>} (an empty base list means burn the base side), PositionRef (Launch(Address), Moment(Address)), TtlPolicy, GradFailure {origin, code} and GraduationOutcome {Graduated(Address), Failed(GradFailure)} (finding V10), LaunchDurations {grace, fallback_delay, rescue_admin, rescue_public, locked_fallback, takeover_delay, takeover_window, timelock, timelock_window, harvest_interval}, MomentsDurations {vest_period, stuck_expiry, pending_backstop, timelock, timelock_window, min_window, max_window, harvest_interval} (no grace: Moments have no mark_stuck, finding F15; pending_backstop is the expiry backstop for a Moment whose graduation never records a failure, finding V11);
  - constants: BPS, ERR_BASE = 10_000 and the ten contract tags of §4 (1 launchpad-v2, 2 launch-token-v2, 3 exec-soroswap, 4 exec-aquarius, 5 qa-exec-fail, 6 lp-locker, 7 moments-v2, 8 moment-nft, 9 moment-coin, 10 moments-graduator) with a const fn err_code(tag, n) = ERR_BASE + tag·100 + n that every v2 contract uses for its #[contracterror] values (finding V10), GRAD_DUST_BPS = 1, MAX_HARVEST_ROUND_BPS = 50, SOROSWAP_MIN_LIQ = 1_000, MIN_DURATION = 60 s, MAX_DURATION = 400 days, MAX_HARVEST_INTERVAL = 1 day, the production duration sets of §14.3 (PRODUCTION_LAUNCH_DURATIONS, PRODUCTION_MOMENTS_DURATIONS) and the testnet-qa sets for tests;
  - validate_launch_durations and validate_moments_durations with the rules of §4 (including fallback_delay ≤ rescue_admin, harvest_interval ≤ MAX_HARVEST_INTERVAL and pending_backstop ≥ 4 · stuck_expiry; harvest_interval is in both sets; findings F6 and V11);
  - #[contractclient] traits for every cross-contract surface (LaunchTokenV2 with notify_reward(notifier, asset, amount) and exclude_treasury(), Executor (error type soroban_sdk::Error, so try_ hands every code over unchanged), Locker with harvest_interval(), HarvestOwner, MomentNft, MomentCoin, Graduator (error type soroban_sdk::Error), TreasurySource, SoroswapFactory, SoroswapPair with token_0/token_1). common/src/aquarius.rs is a stub holding two compile-time flags, AQUARIUS_POOL_LOOKUP_OK and AQUARIUS_VENUE_OK, both false, which CT-03 fills and sets;
  - maths: checked mul_div and mul_div_up, mul_div_u256 and mul_div_up_u256 with a U256 intermediate, isqrt_u128;
  - grad_failure(e) -> GradFailure (finding V10): a contract error in 10_100–11_099 gives origin = (code − ERR_BASE) / 100 and the code; any other contract error (a DEX, a SAC, an OpenZeppelin check) gives origin 0 and the raw code; a host error gives origin 99 and its ScErrorCode.
- Each v2 crate gets a Cargo.toml and a stub lib.rs; ownership passes to its package when CT-00 merges. Add proptest as a dev-dependency where tests need it.
- build.sh builds and spec-shakes all 13 WASMs (3 v1 + 10 v2) into dist/. Do not commit dist; only CT-10 does.
- tools/fetch-fixtures.sh reads a contract's instance through public RPC getLedgerEntries, follows its WASM hash, downloads the code entry into contracts/testdata/, and records {contract id, wasm hash, sha256, network, fetched_at, notes} in testdata/fixtures.json, creating that file if it is missing (CT-03 owns it). It needs no keys and is not run in this package.

Implement §7 (rules for every executor), §7.1 and §7.3 of DESIGN-stellar-contracts-v2.revised.md.
exec-soroswap: __constructor(factory, callers). graduate(GraduateArgs):
- require source ∈ callers (NotCaller) and source.require_auth() (decision L4: only launchpad-v2 and moments-graduator);
- pull both assets from source (pre-authorized by the source);
- create or get the pair; require pair.total_supply() == 0 (PoolNotEmpty, recoverable);
- transfer both amounts straight into the pair, then pair.deposit(lp_to); require liquidity ≥ min_liquidity;
- return any leftovers to source; emit exec_grad.
No storage beyond the instance, no admin, and it never calls its caller.
qa-exec-fail (testnet-qa only, decision O3, §7.3): __constructor(callers, qa_admin, default_mode); set_mode(token, mode) by qa_admin only (NotQaAdmin); unset tokens use default_mode. One instance serves as one venue (no hardcoded venue ids, finding F8) and as the executor of testnet-qa's failing Moments stack (finding F5); its callers are launchpad-v2 and that stack's graduator. Mode 0 returns the recoverable contract error ForcedFailure without moving funds; mode 1 loops until the budget runs out; mode 2 returns a bogus success without moving funds (token_used and quote_used equal to the inputs, its own address as pool and lp_token), which the caller's result checks must reject.
Error enums use dyor-common's err_code: exec-soroswap tag 3, qa-exec-fail tag 5 (so PoolNotEmpty is 10_303 and ForcedFailure 10_502, finding V10).
Tests run against the real Soroswap factory, pair and router WASMs already in contracts/testdata, with a harness contract that calls the executor through try_ and pre-authorizes with authorize_as_current_contract exactly as launchpad-v2 will (§5.5). Confirm SOROSWAP_MIN_LIQ (dyor-common, 1,000) against the pair fixture; report a mismatch to the CT-00 owner instead of editing common.

Implement §12 of DESIGN-stellar-contracts-v2.revised.md. Constructor (moments, coin_wasm_hash, executor, locker, soroswap_factory). graduate(MomentGradArgs{nft, usdc, reserve, pool_coins, name, symbol, expected_coin}):
- moments.require_auth(); any other caller fails NotMoments;
- read moments' USDC balance, then pull the reserve USDC from moments (pre-authorized);
- deploy moment-coin with salt sha256("dyorhq/moment-coin/v2" ‖ nft.to_xdr()) and an initial mint of pool_coins to itself;
- pre-authorize its own transfers and call the executor with lp_to = locker and min_liquidity = isqrt(pool_coins·reserve) − SOROSWAP_MIN_LIQ − 1 (the executor's callers include the graduator, decision L4);
- run the result checks inside its own frame, before any leftover moves (findings F15 and V9): the USDC side (the executor's quote_used within GRAD_DUST_BPS of reserve and ≤ reserve, and equal to the drop in the graduator's USDC balance); the coin side (pool_coins − pool_coins·GRAD_DUST_BPS/BPS ≤ token_used ≤ pool_coins, and the drop in the graduator's coin balance since the mint equals token_used); liquidity ≥ min_liquidity; pool == soroswap_factory.get_pair(coin, usdc); lp_token.balance(locker) ≥ liquidity; coin == expected_coin;
- burn the leftover coins and return the leftover USDC to moments, then check usdc_used + usdc_returned == reserve and that the drop in moments' USDC balance equals usdc_used; return coin_used = token_used;
- a failed check returns the recoverable error GraduationInvalid (ERR_BASE + 10·100 + 3 = 11_003; all errors use tag 10, finding V10), so moments' try_ rolls back the whole frame and records the failure;
- return MomentGradResult.
Also the coin_address(nft) view. Tests call it from a harness through try_, to prove that a failure rolls back the coin deployment. On testnet-qa a second instance with qa-exec-fail as its executor serves the failing Moments stack (finding F5); the code is the same.

Use contractimport! on the real dist WASMs plus the Soroswap and Aquarius fixtures to run §18.2–18.3 of DESIGN-stellar-contracts-v2.revised.md.
Journeys:
- launch → buys → complete → keeper graduate (Soroswap, then Aquarius if CT-03 was a go) → router swaps → harvest → both sides split 50/50: holder claims of quote and launch-token rewards (sharing on), recipient payouts on both sides (sharing off), protocol sweep of both sides (finding F1); the treasury's launch tokens earn no holder rewards, also after a treasury change (finding V2); set_fees after graduation leaves the next harvest's split unchanged (finding V1);
- qa-exec-fail mode 0 → stuck → graduate_fallback refused until fallback_delay → fallback; mode 1 → mark_stuck → fallback; mode 2 → GraduationInvalid abort → mark_stuck → fallback; venue-locked quote → fallback only after the delay or allow_fallback;
- forced failure → admin rescue at 7 d and public rescue at 30 d → pro-rata refunds in random order → full exit;
- a third-party Soroswap pool of a sharing launch → exclude_pool (refused below the floor, accepted above) → stranded owed in both assets to the treasury;
- a recipient change between harvests: the unharvested growth goes to the new recipient (the declared exception, finding F3); with swap volume above the round cap for several intervals, the backlog left after one harvest matches the residual CT-13 reports (finding V7);
- Moments publish → terminal collect → keeper graduate → vesting over 5 periods → harvests with the cap binding (compounded : harvested stays (BPS − hb) : hb = 3,333 : 6,667, coin side burned, finding V3); Moments expiry from Collecting, and from GraduationPending only after a recorded failure (a failing-stack graduator on qa-exec-fail modes 0 and 2); a mode-1 Moment stays pending and expire is refused until completed_at + pending_backstop, then succeeds with the 70/30 split (finding V11);
- the same journeys with the testnet-qa durations of §14.3.
Probes: one re-entry probe per row of §3.3 (including the locker's exclude_treasury call); the error-code probe (an exec-soroswap PoolNotEmpty and an exec-aquarius PaymentUnavailable, and a graduator GraduationInvalid against an executor error, each record a distinct namespaced (origin, code), finding V10); the graduator coin-side probe (a test executor that seeds fewer coins than it reports is rejected, finding V9); squat probes (an attacker calls each executor, transfers the token to a pair, seeds a quote-only pair); the AQUA drain probe; the reward-pool probes (transfers from the token's own address; 50 dust pairs all refused BelowFloor); the SAC-only quote probe; hot-key footprints for launch, buy, sell, refund, publish and collect (§3.5).
Also: stateful property tests across contracts (I-L*, I-T*, I-K1, I-M*), including the compounding ratio; differential vectors against Monad (Launchpad.t.sol curve values including the clamp, MomentsModels.swift maths), scaled for decimals; cost_estimate().resources() ceilings from §18.3, including the worst-case graduate and graduate_fallback per venue and exclude_pool ≤ 60M.
Then build, record dist/SHA256SUMS for all 13 WASMs, and commit dist. Measure the rent per action and report it, replacing the spec's estimates. After a CT-19 fix, rebuild dist so CT-19 can re-review the new hashes.

§20.4 of DESIGN-stellar-contracts-v2.revised.md.
- Allow the new roles. Allow runtime contracts only by pinned WASM hash.
- Bind arguments:
  - launch: creator == user; terms decoded; venue and fallback executors pinned; locker, token hash and durations equal the pins;
  - the XLM launch-fee transfer goes from the user to the pinned launchpad for exactly expected.launch_fee, and expected.launch_fee ≤ the pinned maxLaunchFeeStroops (10 XLM, decision O6, finding F18);
  - refund: holder == user; the burn is the outflow;
  - collect: collector == user and max_total ≤ spend;
  - claim, claim_all, token.claim and claim_owed: account == user with zero spend;
  - permissionless calls carry no user auth.
- Regenerate the shared vectors so the Swift and TypeScript verifiers agree, and keep every old vector passing.

Register the v2 routes and builders: launches, economics, refunds, rewards, owed fees, Moments v2, vesting. v1 routes stay for the retired generation.
Write lite_e2e_v2.ts, which plays the phone and, where needed, the keeper, covering every journey of §18.4 of DESIGN-stellar-contracts-v2.revised.md. It reads every contract id and venue id from deployments/testnet-qa-v2.json and /v1/economics, never from constants (finding F8).
- create with the 10 XLM fee, buy with sharing, complete, keeper graduation (Soroswap; Aquarius, on an XLM quote, only when the deployment file says aquarius.enabled, finding V8), swaps, harvest, quote and launch-token reward claims, creator and owed claims on both sides, protocol sweeps of both sides; the treasury's holder rewards stay 0 (finding V2);
- a failing-venue launch (mode 0) → stuck → graduate_fallback refused before fallback_delay → fallback; a venue-locked launch → allow_fallback and the delay path; mark_stuck after a mode-1 failure; mode 2 → GraduationInvalid at simulation → mark_stuck → fallback; each grad_fail is checked for its namespaced origin and code (finding V10);
- rescue by the QA admin and by a stranger, on two launches; before each completes, insert a lite.keeper_skip row for its token with jobs fallback AND rescue, because the keeper is itself "anyone" and would otherwise graduate it on the fallback or rescue it at rescue_public_at before the stranger (finding V5); pro-rata refunds;
- takeover with veto and execution; treasury, guardian and venue timelocks with a guardian cancel; the guardian handoff;
- Moments on the main stack: publish, collect, terminal, keeper graduation, full vesting with the QA period, harvest, policy timelock; a second Moment left Collecting past its deadline and expired;
- Moments on the failing stack, by direct contract calls signed with QA keys (finding F5): mode 0 → keeper grad_fail → expire after stuck_expiry; mode 2 → the graduator's GraduationInvalid (origin 10, code 11_003) recorded → expire; every Moment the script expires itself gets a keeper_skip row with job expire, so the keeper's optional expiry doesn't race it (finding V5);
- a completed failing-stack Moment without a recorded failure is refused by expire (finding V5): on mode 0 the keeper would record a failure at once, so before its terminal collect insert a keeper_skip row for its NFT address with jobs graduate and expire; after the deadline and past stuck_expiry, expire must fail NotExpirable; then call graduate (the failure is recorded) and expire after stuck_expiry;
- the backstop (finding V11): a mode-1 failing-stack Moment is refused by expire before completed_at + pending_backstop (30 minutes) and expires after it.
Funding (finding F10): the stuck, fallback, rescue and refund journeys use XLM quotes, with one fresh Friendbot buyer per journey; the venue-locked journey uses the QA asset. USDC (Circle USDC) comes from /v1/swap/quote and /v1/swap/build XLM→USDC, as lite_e2e.ts:108-115 does. The amount is computed from the journeys the run includes, not a constant (finding V6): the per-journey needs of spec §18.4 (USDC-quote launch ≈ 44.2, main-stack Moment 13.34, Collecting-expiry Moment ≈ 1, four failing-stack Moments 53.34, harvest swaps ≈ 3; ≈ 114.9 for the full list) times 1.13, which is 130 USDC for the full list. The swap follows a depth check for that amount: quote 1 XLM and the full amount, and require enough output at an average rate within 3% of the 1-XLM rate; otherwise stop the USDC journeys with a clear message and run the XLM ones.
For each state only testnet-qa reaches, the script asserts the API response shape (finding F4).
It refuses to run against any deployment other than testnet-qa (and the local stack pointed at it). Do not run it against a deployment in this package: CT-20 runs it after the CT-19 gate (decision L16), and CT-19 reviews this package first.
